# Mobile Offline Mode

Offline Mode is a **crucial mobile UX feature**, not an edge case. It is a user-forced offline
switch, distinct from the offline-first data layer (SQLite + repositories). The data layer keeps
subscribed content readable without a connection; Offline Mode **refuses the network** and **steers
UI** to downloaded / already-stored views.

## Toggle

- Device-local preference (`offline.mode` in AsyncStorage via `prefs/`). Do **not** sync to the
  account.
- Control lives on **More**, **first under Features** (above overflow tabs / Settings / OPML).
- When on, show description text under the switch explaining that only downloads and other content
  already on the device are available.
- Activation is **toggle-only**. Do **not** auto-enter or auto-leave from NetInfo / airplane mode.

## While on — park all network

- Background sync parks the same way as a real outage (`setNetworkReachable` is false).
- API helpers refuse immediately (no token refresh, no silent retry).
- New downloads are rejected; in-flight transfers pause when the toggle flips on.
- Playback uses a completed local `file://` only — no remote enclosure fallback.

## Screen behavior

- Screens that can work offline **default** to their offline-compatible view (usually
  **Downloaded**). Offline Mode overrides the remembered section/tab on navigate; do not overwrite
  the stored pref. About and other local panes stay selectable after an explicit tap.
- A slim **Offline mode is on** warning strip sits in persistent bottom chrome above the tab bar,
  in order: sync progress → Offline Mode → mini player. It does not slide away on stack push.
- Screens that cannot (Browse global, Search, Home Clips, …) show a dedicated unavailable message —
  never a spinner, empty list, or silent failure.
- Do not auto-switch bottom tabs; the user sees the message on the tab they opened.

## Playback is recorded while parked

Offline listening is persisted device-locally and reconciled when connectivity returns.

- Playback mutations are written to a durable local outbox with meaningful-event timestamps.
- Replay is bounded at 500 events with oldest-first eviction when the cap is reached.
- Position updates collapse to the latest position per item before replay.
- Completion stays sticky across replay so a completed item is not reopened by stale position writes.
- Replay runs once Offline Mode is off and the network is reachable.

